@startuml Jacobi_Step

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 5
skinparam maxMessageSize 150

actor User
participant "System" as System
participant "Connection\nManager" as Connection
participant "Component A\n(Gen 0)" as CompA
participant "Component B\n(Gen 1)" as CompB
participant "IJCSA Solver" as Solver

== Jacobi Co-Simulation Step: step_jacobi(t, dt) ==

User -> System: **step_jacobi(t, dt)**
activate System

note over System: **Phase 1: Set ALL Inputs**\n(for all generations)

loop for each generation in execution_order

    System -> System: generation=[CompA,CompB,...]
    
    note over System: **1.1: Get signals from connections**
    
    System -> Connection: get_incoming_connections(CompB)
    activate Connection
    Connection -> CompA: outputs['y'].get()
    note right: Read from PortState\n(delayed or current)
    CompA --> Connection: value
    Connection --> System: {port: value}
    deactivate Connection
    
    System -> CompB: **set_inputs(signals,t)**
    activate CompB
    CompB -> CompB: inputs['u'].set(value,t)
    note right: Store in PortState\n(does NOT compute yet)
    CompB --> System: inputs set
    deactivate CompB
    
    note over System: **1.2: Check for algebraic loops**
    
    alt generation contains algebraic loop SCC
        System -> Solver: **_solve_algebraic_scc_ijcsa(scc,t)**
        activate Solver
        
        note over Solver: Interface-Newton iteration\nto resolve algebraic coupling
        
        loop until convergence
            Solver -> CompA: evaluate_outputs(inputs,t)
            activate CompA
            CompA -> CompA: compute with dt=0
            CompA --> Solver: output values
            deactivate CompA
            
            Solver -> CompB: evaluate_outputs(inputs,t)
            activate CompB
            CompB -> CompB: compute with dt=0
            CompB --> Solver: output values
            deactivate CompB
            
            Solver -> Solver: compute residual R=U-Y(U)
            Solver -> Solver: compute Jacobian J=dR/dU
            Solver -> Solver: solve J*ΔU=-R
            Solver -> Solver: U+=ΔU
        end
        
        Solver -> CompA: set_inputs(converged_U,t)
        Solver -> CompB: set_inputs(converged_U,t)
        
        Solver --> System: algebraic loop solved
        deactivate Solver
        
        note right: All interface values\nconsistent at time t
    end

end

note over System: **Phase 2: Compute ALL Steps**\n(for all generations)

loop for each generation in execution_order

    System -> System: generation = [CompA,CompB,...]
    
    loop for each component in generation
        System -> CompA: **do_step(t,dt)**
        activate CompA
        CompA -> CompA: _do_step_internal(t,dt)
        note right: FMU doStep / FEM solve\nOpenSim integrate / etc.\nwith t: t -> t+dt
        CompA -> CompA: t = t + dt
        CompA -> CompA: _update_output_states(t+dt)
        note right: Write new outputs\n+ append to history
        CompA --> System: step complete
        deactivate CompA
    end
    
end

System --> User: step complete
deactivate System

' note over System
' **Key Differences from Gauss-Seidel:**
' - Phase 1 and Phase 2 are FULLY separated
' - All inputs set before ANY computation
' - Components in same generation can be
'   computed in parallel (Phase 2)
' - Algebraic loops still solved via IJCSA
'   in Phase 1 for consistency
' end note

@enduml